<title>UK: Northwest Europe oil, gas rigs up two on week at 6.</title>
<headline>Northwest Europe oil, gas rigs up two on week at 6.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of active oil and gas rigs operating  offshore Northwest Europe totalled 63 in the week ending July 30,  up two from the previous week, consultants Arthur Andersen said.</p>
<p>There were 27 rigs drilling in the UK sector, one down on last week,  while Norway was steady at 17. The Danish and Irish sectors were both  up one at four each while the Netherlands was one up at 11.</p>
<p>Arthur Andersen said that near the end of July, there were 60 percent  more exploration and appraisal spuds, sidetracks and re-entries throughout  Northwest Europe than in the corresponding period of 1996.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7630</p>
